# NEOCOM workspace

Each repository is one independent project. The parent `neocom` repository is deprecated. Do not treat the others as its submodules, and do not update submodule pointers.

Active projects:

| Folder | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `neocom-meta` | Docs, programme definition, Cursor rules/skills, OpenSpec, and subagents ([AdamAntinoo/neocom-meta](https://github.com/AdamAntinoo/neocom-meta.git)) |
| `neocom-front` | Frontend application ([AdamAntinoo/neocom-front](https://github.com/AdamAntinoo/neocom-front.git)) |
| `neocom-back` | Backend application ([AdamAntinoo/neocom-back](https://github.com/AdamAntinoo/neocom-back.git)) |
| `neocom-domain` | Published Node domain library on npm ([AdamAntinoo/neocom-domain](https://github.com/AdamAntinoo/neocom-domain.git)). Package version is **npm-led** (`npm run version:sync` from latest publish); git tags follow after publish |

Left aside for now: `neocom` and `neocom-esi`.

## Node

Every NEOCOM repository has `.nvmrc` set to the nvm alias `neocom`. Before `node`, `npm`, or `npx`, run `nvm use` in that repository. Do not select a Node version by number.

## Front stack

- Latest Angular + TypeScript
- Unit tests: Vitest (Angular CLI default)
- Acceptance tests: Cypress with Cucumber

## Ecosystem tools

In `neocom-meta`:

- **OpenSpec** — spec-driven planning and change workflow (`openspec` CLI; Cursor integration via `openspec init --tools cursor`)
- **Graphify** — code-knowledge graph for Cursor (`graphify` CLI from package `graphifyy`)

See `.cursor/rules/neocom-ecosystem-tools.mdc` for install and usage notes.

## Delegation

Use these project subagents proactively:

- `/neocom-methodology` — design, spec, develop, test, and deploy across repositories. Epics start at L1. See section 5 of `PROGRAMME.md`
- `/neocom-code` — product code and OpenSpec application in `neocom-front`, `neocom-back`, and `neocom-domain`
- `/neocom-meta` — docs, agent config, and spec pipeline in `neocom-meta`
- `/neocom-git` — commits, PRs, releases, and promotions for one independent repository. OpenSpec feature apply commits on `feature/<feature>` from `develop`. After the user reviews and tests, open a pull request into `develop`. Archive opens a pull request from `develop` into `main` titled `Release-` plus GitVersion `MajorMinorPatch` (apps/meta). For **`neocom-domain`**, package version follows npm (see `/neocom-git` Versioning)
- `/git:commit <project>` — commit all pending changes on that repository's current branch through `/neocom-git`. Project is required (`neocom-meta`, `neocom-front`, `neocom-back`, or `neocom-domain`)
- `/git:pr` — commit pending work and prepare pull requests through `/neocom-git`. `/git:pr <project>` selects one active repository (`neocom-meta`, `neocom-front`, `neocom-back`, or `neocom-domain`). No project applies to `neocom-meta`, `neocom-front`, and `neocom-back` (domain is opt-in by name). `neocom` and `neocom-esi` stay aside
- `/epic` — open an L1 epic under `05.REQUIREMENTS-DECOMPOSITION/L1/`
- `/neo:extract-l2` — Convert L1 epics into epic-named L2 file(s). No args: pending epics; args: named epics only. The current L2 tree marks what is already generated
- `/neo:spec-evolution` — review L2 notes and move them into OpenSpec; optional L2 paths limit the run to those files
- `/feature-delivery` — branch `feature/<feature>` from `develop`, commit, then wait for user review before the pull request into `develop`. Several features can be open, rebase when one needs another, and share one pull request. See section 5.9 of `PROGRAMME.md`
- `/verifier` — readonly check after work is claimed done

Keep each change inside the folder that owns it. Do not implement frontend features in meta or back, or backend features in meta or front. Domain library code stays in `neocom-domain`.

When `neocom-front` is missing or empty, use the recorded front stack (do not re-ask). When `neocom-back` is missing or empty, ask which backend stack and repository to use before scaffolding.

Requirements flow: `/neocom-methodology` / `/epic` writes L1, then `/neo:extract-l2` into L2, then `/neo:spec-evolution` into OpenSpec, then `/feature-delivery` when applying a feature. There is no `/spec-collect` and no `02.SOURCES` intake. See `.cursor/rules/neocom-spec-pipeline.mdc` and section 5 of `PROGRAMME.md`.

Programme docs: keep `01.PROGRAMME-DEFINITION/` current (architecture + active features such as Initialization and Login) as inputs and development produce durable decisions.
